# Build-context excludes for `-f relay/PushRelay/Dockerfile` (BuildKit reads
# `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the context root's file). The
# context is the repo root — this image needs `relay/PushRelay`,
# `services/MomoMetrics`, and LICENSE/NOTICE; everything else is weight.
#
# It is a superset of the repo-root `.dockerignore`, because when this file
# exists it REPLACES that one: every secret-bearing pattern there is repeated
# here. If a builder ignores per-Dockerfile ignore files, the root
# `.dockerignore` applies instead and the build still succeeds (larger context).
#
# Same structure as server-rust/Dockerfile.dockerignore.

# --- never in any image context (mirrors the repo root .dockerignore) --------
.git
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.secret.env
**/*.secrets.env
infra/prod/secrets.env
infra/prod/*.sops.env
infra/prod/*.plain.env
infra/prod/*.decrypted
infra/prod/age.key
infra/prod/keys.txt
local-gate-evidence

# An APNs key must never be reachable from a build context. The relay receives
# its `.p8` as a runtime mount and this image is built without one; these
# patterns make "accidentally committed next to the checkout" unbuildable rather
# than silently baked into a layer (ADR-0120 D1-A).
**/*.p8
**/*.p12
**/*.mobileprovision
push-relay-keys
**/*-ed25519-private.pem

# --- build output ------------------------------------------------------------
target
**/target
.build
**/.build
**/.swiftpm
**/DerivedData
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__

# --- trees this image never copies -------------------------------------------
adapters
clients
docs
examples
fastlane
infra
legal
packages
research
scripts
server
server-rust
workers
relay/OutboxRelay
services/CloudProviderKit
services/LinkShort
services/OutboundHTTPPolicy
BUILD_TICKETS.md
ROADMAP.md
STATUS.md
schema_v0.sql
Gemfile
Makefile
package.json
package-lock.json
